              <span class="check-num">20</span>
              <span class="check-title">A reusable intake rule is written and tested</span>
            </label>
            <div class="check-detail">Evidence looks like: the "until ___" sentence contains an observable gate, and today's three catches all fail at that gate. A gate you cannot observe is not a gate.</div>
          </li>

          <li class="check-item" data-check-item data-outcome-after="pulse-log">
            <label class="check-label">
              <input type="checkbox" id="p5-mvp-contain" name="p5-mvp-contain" data-check-id="mvp-contain" />
              <span class="check-num">21</span>
              <span class="check-title">The final decision rests on containment evidence</span>
            </label>
            <div class="check-detail">Evidence looks like: the log's verdict resting on artifacts. Before/after manifest receipts, target checks, quarantine listing. With no load-bearing reassurance from the assistant. A reviewer can reach the same decision from those artifacts alone.</div>
          </li>

          <li class="check-item" data-check-item data-outcome-after="#p5-transfer-outcome-point">
            <label class="check-label">
              <input type="checkbox" id="p5-p5-transfer" name="p5-p5-transfer" data-check-id="p5-transfer" />
              <span class="check-num">22</span>
              <span class="check-title">The P5 transfer rule is recorded and dated</span>
            </label>
            <div class="check-detail">Evidence looks like: the three fields under <strong>From P5 — Operating picture</strong> in <code>operator/TRANSFER_30_60_90.md</code> contain today's date, the trusted knowledge boundary at work, the intake rule in its "never accept into trusted until ___" form, and the first corpus or inbox it applies to. An entry naming a category rather than a system you could put a gate in front of on Monday is a not-yet.</div>
          </li>
